<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">The Basics of HTML</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p>First let's start off with what HTML is. HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. This may seem like random words, but it does have meaning behind it. HyperText, the 'HT', simply refers to text that has links, references, and other extra aspects that regular text may not have. Markup Language, the 'ML', is a shorthand way of saying that the language itself can change and give structure to the HyperText. </p>
<p>HTML is mostly composed of tags. Tags is what gives structure and order to the document, and allows you to give special meaning to each element. Tags are defined like the following: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;tag&gt; &lt;/tag&gt;</span>". Before we get into structure, let us go over basic tags and what they do.</p>
<p>Tags typically have an opening and closing of them. An opening is simply the name encapsulated with a less than and greater than symbol like so: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;tag&gt;</span>". Tags are then closed in a similar fashion, but with a slash before the tag's name, like so: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;/tag&gt;</span>". This is useful as you can put content in between the start and closing tag.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>Understand what HTML stands for.</li>
<li>Understand what HTML means.</li>
<li>Understand what a tag is in HTML and how it is formatted.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Complete the fill-in-the-blanks activity below from what you've learnt in the block of code above. Then, continue with this section.</p>
</div>
</div>
