<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">The Basic Tags of HTML</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p>Here are some basic tags and what they do:</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;p&gt;</span> - Stands for "paragraph," allows you to put simple, regular text. Example: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;p&gt;This is paragraph text!&lt;/p&gt;</span>"</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;h1&gt;</span> - Stands for "header," with the 1 signifying it's the largest type of header. Numbers range from 1-6, with a smaller number leading to a smaller header. Example: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;h2&gt;This Is a Header!&lt;/h2&gt;</span>"</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;title&gt;</span> - Stands for "title," titles your webpage, and is typically found at the head / top of your document. Example: "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;title&gt;This is a title&lt;/title&gt;</span>"</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;head&gt;<span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">, </span>&lt;body&gt;</span> - Separate, but main sections of your document, with different parts going into each. More information on the next sub module.</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;div&gt;</span> - Stands for "division", allows for grouping and advanced structure.</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">&lt;html&gt;</span> - Main section, all other tags should be placed within this one, everything within is defined as part of the document, though, more will be discussed during the next section.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>Understand how the given tag structure applies to HTML.</li>
<li>Remember some of the basic tags in HTML.</li>
<li>Know how to use said basic tags of HTML.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Complete the matching activity that matches different tags to the common tag name below to complete this submodule using what you know from the given tag information above and from the other activity in this submodule.</p>
</div>
</div>
