<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">One More Style Option</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p style="font-size: 17px;">There is one more single style modifier that should be known that has a special importance. That's inline style, where the style is directly in the HTML item like so:<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace; color: #0f172a; font-size: 16px;">&lt;p style="color:red;"&gt; This is my text! &lt;/p&gt;</span></p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0f172a; font-size: 16px;">This is important because of it's priority listing. It falls between the !important tag and an id css ruling in terms of important, meaning it will override anything unless there is a !important tag on something that changes its style.</span></p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #0f172a; font-size: 16px;">Let's take a look at one last activity before wrapping this submodule up.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>What is an inline style in CSS.</li>
<li>The priority ranking of an inline style.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
