<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Further Things to Note</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p>Typically, elements and tags in HTML documents are given either classes or ids in order to style them, with classes being the most prevalent since it works well with JavaScript, which we will get into in its own section.</p>
<p>One thing to note though is if there are two things of the same priority, whatever is lower on the list will be the style that is applied.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>CSS in relation to the future subject of the course.</li>
<li>How styles with the same priority interact.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Change things in both the HTML tab and CSS tab in the code editor below to test out some styles and it relates to HTML.</p>
</div>
</div>
