<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Add Colors and Fonts</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p style="font-size: 17px;">Last section, the basics of CSS was covered. Now, it's time to talk about the colors and fonts that CSS can set. These texts can be paragraphs, headers, or even applied to the parent of a text element that it can then apply to. Here is a list of some basic things you can change for a text that can be set by CSS.</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">color</span>: Can add color to a text, by either giving any color value.<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-family</span>: Changes the font of a text.<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-size</span>: Changes the size of a font given a value.<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-style</span>: Can give a font a style, like italics.<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-weight</span>: Can bold a font given a value from 100-1000, with a higher value being bolder.<br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">text-decoration</span>: Can add decor like an underline or strikethrough.</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">That's generally it, but a few extra tips:<br /></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-size: 17px;">A color value can be given by things like a hex value ('#FF0000'), an rgb ('rgb(255, 0, 0)'), an hsl ('hsl(0, 100%, 50%)'), or just by name ('red').</li>
<li style="font-size: 17px;">The <span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-family</span> property can be given a chain of fonts separated by commas, so if the first one fails to be loaded, it will load the next one in line. Make sure to use web-safe fonts, or fonts that most computers can recognize and has the files for!</li>
<li style="font-size: 17px;">The <span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">font-weight</span> property can also be given a name value as well, like 'bold'.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>Use font size and line height to support readability.</li>
<li>Ensure that your text is proper when styled.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Complete the activities determining your knowledge on CSS properties and text readability.</p>
