<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Add Spacing and Page Layout</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p style="font-size: 17px;">Spacing and layout turn a collection of elements into an organized page. Margin creates space outside an element, while padding creates space inside its border. The box-sizing property can make widths easier to predict. In the project, generous padding keeps text away from card edges, while margins separate one section from another. These choices create visual grouping without adding extra HTML.</p>
<p>Layout also needs to respond to available space. A max-width keeps long text from stretching across an extremely wide monitor, while automatic left and right margins center the content. Images can use width: 100% and height: auto so they scale with their container. A media query can reduce padding on a narrow screen. Responsive design does not require a completely different mobile page; it adapts the same content.</p>
<p>The CSS below also adds rounded corners and a subtle shadow to the content sections. Those details are optional decoration, but the spacing and responsive width directly support usability. Try not to solve layout with repeated <br> elements or spaces in HTML. Use CSS because spacing is a presentation decision.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>Margin = outside space; padding = inside space.</li>
<li>Use max-width to keep reading lines comfortable.</li>
<li>Make images flexible instead of forcing a large fixed width.</li>
<li>Use media queries for targeted narrow-screen adjustments.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Complete the activity below using what you know about margins and padding so far before moving onto the next text.</p>
</div>
</div>
