<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">More on Page Layout and Spacing</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p style="font-size: 17px;">Another thing that can be used is using a flexbox. By applying 'flex' to display, then by applying a 'flex direction,' you can then style it by using things like "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">justify-content</span>" and "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">align-items</span>", which can be set to center to automatically center things. Justify content goes by major axis and aligning goes by the minor axis, which is set by the flex direction.</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">Another way is by setting margin to auto on its sides. When margin is given two values, it applies the first value is applied to the top and bottom, while the second value is applied to the left and right. For example, '<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">margin: 0px auto;<span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">'</span></span> sets the top and bottom to nothing, but automatically setting the left and right to center it. Do note, that the 'auto' keyword does different things to different items, make sure to search what it does in certain contexts or test it out to see what it does.</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">Additionally, when you get more advanced, you can use media queries to set special CSS rules for when things get certain sizes.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>Know how to use margins and padding to your pages benefit.</li>
<li>Remember to know how to style your content.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Change the section padding, maximum content width, and mobile breakpoint. Resize the browser and watch the same HTML adapt.</p>
</div>
</div>
