<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family: Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; line-height: 1.62; color: #0f172a; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">What JavaScript Adds to the Page</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card">
<p style="font-size: 17px;">While you've learnt HTML and CSS, or the base and style of a page, there is one more piece. Interactability, which belongs to JavaScript. JavaScript is a programming language which can give your website a bit more flare. For example, remember classes from earlier?</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">JavaScript can change the class of things, and by extension, the style, which applies immediately. Here's an example of that in action!</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">document.getElementById("elementId").classList.remove("classA");</span><br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">document.getElementById("elementId").classList.add("classB");</span></p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">This code does a lot, so allow it to be broken down. First 'document' refers to the document the script is called from. Next, 'getElementById' is a function that given a valid Id, it will pull that element in the code. Finally, the 'classList' part access that element's class list and removes, then adds different classes via their respective functions. It also could have been written as so:</p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">let myElement = document.getElementById("elementId");</span><br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">myElement.classList.remove("classA");</span><br /><span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">myElement.classList.add("classB");</span></p>
<p style="font-size: 17px;">This time, it uses the "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">let</span>" variable to assign that element to a variable called "<span style="font-family: 'courier new', courier, monospace;">myElement</span>," then using the variable to access its class list and change it there.</p>
</div>
<div class="figma-info-grid">
<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 22px;">
<li>JavaScript can change the behaviors of a page.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 360px; background: #ecfeff; border: 1px solid #99f6e4; border-radius: 13px; padding: 17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: #115e59;">Your task</h2>
<p style="margin: 0;">Read the JavaScript activity below to learn more about JavaScript.</p>
</div>
</div>
