<div class="figma-page-content" style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.62;color:#0f172a;max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;">
<h1 class="figma-screen-title">Find and Fix Common Beginner Errors</h1>
<div class="figma-reading-card"><p style="font-size:17px;">Small errors are normal in webpage development. HTML problems often come from missing closing tags, misplaced quotation marks, or content placed outside the intended container. CSS problems often come from a selector that does not match the HTML, a misspelled property, or a missing punctuation mark. JavaScript problems often come from an incorrect element ID, a missing parenthesis or brace, or code that runs against an element it cannot find.</p><p>A useful debugging strategy is to identify the symptom, choose the most likely layer, and reduce the problem. If the whole section disappears, start with HTML. If the section exists but a color does not apply, start with CSS. If the button appears but does not respond, start with JavaScript. Compare exact names and test after every repair instead of making several guesses at once.</p><p>The editor below intentionally contains beginner mistakes. The page heading tag is incomplete, the CSS selector uses the wrong class name, and JavaScript requests an ID that does not exist. Repair one error at a time and run after each fix. The goal is not speed; it is developing a repeatable troubleshooting process you can use on your own page.</p></div>
<div class="figma-info-grid" style="">
<div style="flex:1 1 440px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;">Key ideas</h2><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:22px;"><li>Read the symptom before editing.</li><li>Check the responsible layer first.</li><li>Compare IDs and selectors exactly.</li><li>Fix one problem, run, and then move to the next.</li></ul>
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 360px;background:#ecfeff;border:1px solid #99f6e4;border-radius:13px;padding:17px 19px;">
<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115e59;">Your task</h2><p style="margin:0;">Repair the broken heading, make the CSS style the intended card, and make the button update the message.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin:22px 0;"><iframe loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups" src="{{context_path}}/content/resources/embeds/screen-18-editor-01.html" style="width:100%;height:680px;border:0;border-radius:14px;background:#f8fafc;display:block;" title="Interactive code editor: Debugging Practice"></iframe></div>
<details style="margin:22px 0;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:#0f766e;">Quick check: What is the safest way to debug several problems?</summary>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;">Fix and test one small problem at a time, beginning with the layer that matches the symptom.</p>
</details>
<div class="figma-footer-line" style="padding-top:13px;border-top:1px solid #e2e8f0;color:#64748b;font-size:13px;">Basics in Webpage Making · Screen 18 of 20</div>
